[('State a falsifiable relationship.','For a uniform material, measured mass versus sample volume can be modelled as m = ρV + b. The slope tests density; the intercept can reveal a container offset. A hypothesis should predict a pattern that competing explanations might fail to predict.'),('Separate repeatability from validity.','Independent repeated trials reduce uncertainty in the mean roughly as 1/√N when the variation has a stable finite variance. They do not remove a shared calibration offset. A controlled experiment changes one relevant variable while checking plausible confounders.'),('Interpret a rate proxy carefully.','In the sample magnesium–acid lab, reciprocal completion time is proportional to an average extent rate only when the same reaction extent is reached in every trial. A few times at different temperatures do not establish a universal maximum rate.')],
'm_measured = ρV + b; average progress rate = Δξ/Δt',
'If equal Mg pieces complete reaction in 40 s and 20 s, the second has twice the average progress rate under the same completion criterion. It need not have twice the instantaneous rate at every moment.',
