[('Introduce a mole-sized sample.','Write m = nM and V = nV_m. Dividing cancels n, giving ρ = M/V_m. This explains why density depends on both particle mass and packing.'),('Connect temperature to density.','At fixed mass, increasing volume lowers density. Differentiating ln ρ = ln m − ln V at fixed pressure gives d ln ρ/dT = −β. This is a local relationship, not a universal constant-density rule.'),('Recover a gas-density equation.','For a gas V_m = ZRT/P, so ρ = PM/(ZRT). The ideal-gas expression follows only when Z is sufficiently close to one.')],
'ρ = M/V_m; (∂lnρ/∂T)p = −β; ρ_gas = PM/(ZRT)',
