[('Read the carbonyl’s polarization.','A C=O bond places electron density unevenly and creates a relatively electrophilic carbon. Nucleophilic addition at an aldehyde or ketone can be understood as forming a bond to that carbon while redistributing π density toward oxygen.'),('Compare related groups using resonance.','A carboxylate ion distributes negative charge over two oxygen atoms in the symmetric limiting description, stabilizing the conjugate base. An amide lone pair interacts with the adjacent carbonyl system, giving the C–N bond partial double-bond character and changing nitrogen basicity compared with an ordinary amine.'),('Connect structure with acid strength and physical behaviour.','A lower free-energy cost for proton transfer corresponds to a larger K_a. Hydrogen bonding, solvent stabilization, inductive effects, and molecular size all matter; naming a functional group does not supply an entire quantitative reactivity ranking.')],
'HA + B ⇌ A⁻ + BH⁺\nK_transfer = K_a(HA)/K_a(BH⁺) = 10^[pK_a(BH⁺) − pK_a(HA)]',
